@Transactional
public TaskView startTask(String incidentKey, String taskKey, String actor, TaskStartRequest req) {
    String requestId = requireText(req.requestId(), "requestId");
    if (req.expectedTaskVersion() == null) throw badRequest;
    Incident incident = lockIncident(incidentKey);
    requireCommander(incident, actor);
    return runIdempotent(requestId, "task_start", structuredHash(...), TaskView.class, () -> {
        IncidentTask task = ...;
        if (task.status() != OPEN) → 409 (terminal) or 422 (STARTED already)? STARTED → conflict 409 "任务已开始"? Idempotent replay handles same requestId. Different requestId starting twice → 409 conflict. I'll use conflict for STARTED/DONE/CANCELLED here ("任务已处于非 OPEN 状态").
        Hmm — but spec says start failures are 422 for "not in window or deps unmet". Status conflict → 409 consistent with existing style.
        if (task.version() != expected) → 409
        TaskAssignment assignment = assignments.findByTaskId(task.id()).orElseThrow(() → unprocessable("任务没有执行安排，不能开始", null));
        Instant now = now();
        if (now.isBefore(assignment.startAt()) || !now.isBefore(assignment.endAt())) → 422 details {date, windowStart, windowEnd, now}
        List<String> unresolved = unresolvedBlockers(task.id());
        if (!unresolved.isEmpty()) → 422 with details list
        int updated = tasks.markStarted(task.id(), expectedVersionInt, actor, now);
        if (updated == 0) throw conflict 版本或状态已变化
        return toTaskView(...);
    });
}
```

cancelAssignment:

```java
@Transactional
public TaskView cancelAssignment(...) {
    validate requestId, expectedTaskVersion
    lockIncident, requireCommander
    runIdempotent(requestId, "task_assignment_cancel", hash, TaskView.class, () -> {
        task = ...;
        if terminal → 409; if STARTED → 422 已开始不可改时
        version check → 409
        assignments.lockAssignments();  // 与 schedule 串行（删除影响他人校验？删除只释放，但为一致性加锁）
        var existing = assignments.findByTaskId(task.id());
        if (existing.isEmpty()) → 404? or 409 "任务没有安排". Use conflict 409.
        assignments.deleteByTaskId(task.id());
        bumpVersionIfOpen → check 1
        return toTaskView;
    });
}
```

completeTask changes:

```java
if (task.status() != TaskStatus.OPEN && task.status() != TaskStatus.STARTED) → 409 终态
var assignment = assignments.findByTaskId(task.id());
if (assignment.isPresent() && task.status() != TaskStatus.STARTED) {
    throw unprocessable("任务已安排但未开始，完成前必须先开始", null);
}
unresolved blockers check (existing)
tasks.markDone(...)
```

cancelTask changes:

```java
if (task.status() != OPEN && task.status() != STARTED) → 409
if (task.status() == OPEN) {
    assignments.lockAssignments()? 
    assignments.deleteByTaskId(task.id());  // 释放未开始安排
}
tasks.markCancelled(...)
```

For delete in cancelTask — do I need the global lock? Deleting releases capacity; concurrent schedule validation could read stale... With row lock on incident only, another event's schedule for same assignee could compute based on the assignment still present (conservative, fine) or after delete (fine). The dangerous direction is insertion, which is serialized by assignment_lock. Deletion without lock is safe (only makes constraints looser). But to be consistent I'll lock in cancelAssignment (explicit release endpoint) — actually not needed either. Keep it simple: no lock on delete paths. Hmm, but consider: schedule validates person P has assignment A1 (from task T1) 23:00-01:00. Concurrently T1 (OPEN) is cancelled, deleting A1. Schedule commits with constraint based on A1 — conservative, still valid after A1 deleted. Fine, no lock needed for deletes.

But wait — cancelTask deletes assignment for OPEN task. What about version bump? markCancelled does version+1. Good.

createTask: `new IncidentTask(0L, incident.id(), taskKey, groupCode, title, TaskStatus.OPEN, 1, actor, null, null, null, null, null, null, now, now)`.

toTaskView:

```java
private TaskView toTaskView(IncidentTask task) {
    List<TaskBlockerView> blockers = ...;
    AssignmentView assignment = assignments.findByTaskId(task.id())
            .map(a -> new AssignmentView(a.assignee(), a.startAt(), a.endAt())).orElse(null);
    return new TaskView(task.taskKey(), task.groupCode(), task.title(), task.status().name(),
            task.version(), blockers, task.createdBy(), task.createdAt(), assignment,
            task.startedBy(), task.startedAt(), task.doneBy(), task.doneAt(),
            task.cancelledBy(), task.cancelledAt());
}
```

structuredHash:

```java
private String structuredHash(String operation, List<Object> parts) {
    try {
        List<Object> identity = new ArrayList<>();
        identity.add(operation);
        identity.addAll(parts);
        return hash(objectMapper.writeValueAsString(identity));
    } catch (JsonProcessingException e) {
        throw new IllegalStateException("幂等身份序列化失败", e);
    }
}
```

And hash(String) single-arg overload: existing hash(String...) — call hash(json) works with varargs.

Wait, "身份含操作、操作者、资源及全部参数和期望版本" — operation included, actor included, resource (incidentKey/taskKey) included, all params + expected version. Good.

Note: runIdempotent already compares operation separately, but including in hash is harmless.

Instant serialization by objectMapper: default Spring Boot ObjectMapper has JavaTimeModule; Instant serializes as decimal timestamp or ISO string depending on config (WRITE_DATES_AS_TIMESTAMPS default true in Spring Boot? Spring Boot disables WRITE_DATES_AS_TIMESTAMPS by default → ISO-8601 string). Either way deterministic. But to be safe I'll pass instants as strings (toString) in the identity list.

Now — permission before replay: for new endpoints I do requireCommander before runIdempotent. But note runIdempotent replays stored response — if commander changed between first call and replay (handover), the new commander replaying someone else's requestId gets 409 permission. That's the intended "权限先于重放".

Edge: lockIncident → requireCommander → runIdempotent. requireCommander throws 409 conflict. Good.

Now version comparisons: req.expectedTaskVersion() is Long; task.version() int. `if (task.version() != req.expectedTaskVersion())` — auto-unbox long vs int comparison works via widening. I'll capture `long expectedVersion = req.expectedTaskVersion();` and compare `task.version() != expectedVersion`. And markStarted/bumpVersionIfOpen take int — cast `(int) expectedVersion` after validating range? expectedVersion could be huge; if != task.version() we throw 409 before cast. If equal, cast is safe. OK.

Also need imports in IncidentService: Duration, LocalDate, ZoneOffset, Comparator, HashMap, AssignmentRequest, AssignmentCancelRequest, TaskStartRequest, AssignmentView, detail records.

